    <string name="how_it_works_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_body">When a Short or Reel is detected, Anti Scroll presses Back and displays a focus reminder. Nothing you view is stored or sent.</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_punitive_body">When a Short or Reel is detected, the entire platform is blocked for 30 minutes. Attempts during the penalty display the remaining time.</string>
    <string name="privacy_badge">100% local · No Internet permission</string>
    <string name="disclosure_title">Before continuing</string>
    <string name="disclosure_body">Anti Scroll uses Android accessibility access only to identify whether YouTube Shorts or Instagram Reels is visible. It uses Back to leave blocked content or a sanctioned application without changing the current launcher page, and prevents access to the platform for 30 minutes in punitive mode. Interface content is never stored or transmitted.</string>
